    {
      "event": "reviewed",
      "id": 5728198555,
      "node_id": "PRR_kwDOAN28mc8AAAABVW1fmw",
      "url": null,
      "actor": null,
      "commit_id": "adbc31fe33e087c12c5eba655607b6b2a2788423",
      "commit_url": null,
      "created_at": null,
      "updated_at": "2026-11-01T13:04:59Z",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "I loaded the file and checked it against my own BIP 360 work. The depth coverage is solid. There is a passing control block at the maximum depth of 128 with the matching reject at 129. The small end is covered down to a single leaf. The reject set with stable error ids reads clean.\n\nOne gap on the passing side. The six valid inputs sign with SIGHASH_DEFAULT and SIGHASH_ALL only. SIGHASH_SINGLE, SIGHASH_NONE and the ANYONECANPAY variants are the flags that change which sighash midstate is used, so with none of them in a passing case an implementation that selects the wrong midstate for those flags would still pass every vector. Worth adding a few inputs that exercise them. I can send the signed inputs if that helps.",
      "user": {
        "login": "quantova-inc",
        "id": 194181239,
        "node_id": "U_kgDOC5L4dw",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/194181239?v=4",
