      "parents": [
        {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bips/git/commits/b31410ca587cec1cfd880b6617cc6b7cb036e6d7",
          "sha": "b31410ca587cec1cfd880b6617cc6b7cb036e6d7",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/commit/b31410ca587cec1cfd880b6617cc6b7cb036e6d7"
        }
      ],
      "message": "bip360: add spend-path test vectors\n\nThe existing vectors are construction-only, so implementations have to\ninvent their own spend coverage. This adds a spending file in the shape\nof bip-0341/wallet-test-vectors.json, adapted to an output type whose\nonly spend path is the script path.\n\nTwo transactions cover the valid cases, each with the five shared\nBIP 341 sighash hashes at the group level and per-input given,\nintermediary and expected fields. The first has six inputs and signs\nonly with SIGHASH_DEFAULT and SIGHASH_ALL, the second has five, one for\neach of the other hash types. A separate invalidSpending array has ten\nself-contained transactions that must fail validation, with the reason\nin a short spec-level error string.\n\nPrivate keys are sha256(\"p2mr_spending/key/<n>\"), prevout txids are\nsha256(\"p2mr_spending/prevout/<n>\") in internal byte order, and signing\nis BIP 340 with an all-zero aux, so the signatures can be re-derived\nrather than trusted. Two of the inputs reuse trees from\np2mr_construction.json, which makes the two files cross-check each\nother.",
